    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0769" n="669" xml:id="pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72114/5167: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-10T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Presumably you have received from our Legation in Denmark its telegram to the
                    Department No. 5 of January 7, 2 p.m. in regard to the mission of O’Grady. In
                    case you have not received this telegram inform that Legation that it is the
                    desire of the Department that this and all further messages on the subject be
                    repeated to you.</p>
                <p>In case the negotiations by O’Grady may involve, as suggested, the repatriation
                    from Russia of others than British subjects, the Department desires that you
                    present to the British Government the question of including Americans in any
                    arrangement that may be made.</p>
                <p>According to the information which this Department has at present, the Americans
                    involved are Mr. Kalamatiano<anchor n="58" xml:id="d802-f1"/> and Mrs.
                        Doty.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d802-f2"/> The American Government also has an
                    interest, however, in securing the release of Mrs. Kennedy, Miss Loviaguine, and
                    Miss Karin Sante.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d802-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d802-f1" n="58" xml:id="d802-f1-content">
                <p>Former employee of the consulate general at Moscow.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d802-f2" n="59" xml:id="d802-f2-content">
                <p>Wife of Consul William F. Doty.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d802-f3" n="60" xml:id="d802-f3-content">
                <p>Former employees of the Embassy and consulate at Petrograd.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
